# @ryph/forge — environment for the forge process (`bun run dev`): the read-only git
# gateway agent containers clone through, the bundle intake their work leaves by, and the
# GitHub App and GitLab boundary. Runs as its own process in EVERY deployment — the control plane's side
# of the pairing (RYPH_FORGE_URL, RYPH_GIT_GATEWAY_URL) is configured over there.
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and adjust.

# ── Listener ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#RYPH_FORGE_PORT=7412

# ── Control plane ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both REQUIRED: the gateway resolves each run's presented git credential by calling the
# orchestrator, authenticating with the shared service token — without them it can serve no one.
# The token must match the control plane's RYPH_FORGE_TOKEN.
#RYPH_ORCHESTRATOR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7411
#RYPH_FORGE_TOKEN=

# Door ⑤, the agents' issue and pull request tools: the credential the mcp-gateway presents on
# /v1/forge-mcp (the gateway's RYPH_FORGE_GATEWAY_TOKEN). Needs a forge below (the GitHub App,
# GitLab or Radicle). Unset: dark.
#RYPH_FORGE_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# ── Data root ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One directory, three concerns: cache/ (bare clones — disposable), patches/ (the saved
# bundles — the real output, guard it like a database), staging/ (scratch — wiped on boot).
#RYPH_FORGE_DATA=forge-data

# ── GitHub App ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The App behind installation listings, permission checks, PR submission, and OAuth exchange.
# Configure ALL FOUR credentials or none — a partial set fails the boot. With none set, this
# surface stays dark and the git gateway + bundle intake serve as normal.
# Every environment needs its OWN App. An App has one Setup URL — where GitHub sends people after
# they install it — so a shared App lands one environment's installs on the other one's address.
#RYPH_GITHUB_APP_ID=
# The App's private key: either a path to the downloaded .pem or the PEM inline.
#RYPH_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=
#RYPH_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY=
#RYPH_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
#RYPH_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# API and OAuth base URLs — override only for GitHub Enterprise or a test double.
#RYPH_GITHUB_API=https://api.github.com
#RYPH_GITHUB_OAUTH=https://github.com

# ── GitLab ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One instance, gitlab.com unless named (a path prefix is fine; GitLab 17.0 or newer). `bot`, the
# default, acts as a bot user added to projects at the Developer role, with webhooks, sign-in and
# a sign-up group; `user` acts as one person and takes none of those (merges are polled). The
# token needs the scopes api, read_repository and write_repository: RYPH_GITLAB_TOKEN, or
# RYPH_GITLAB_TOKEN_COMMAND (a command printing it; refused where RYPH_FORGE_NO_TOKEN_COMMAND=1,
# as in the forge image), e.g. glab's credential helper, which renews glab's 2-hour OAuth token:
#   printf 'protocol=https\nhost=gitlab.com\n\n' | glab auth git-credential get | sed -n 's/^password=//p'
# A partial set fails the boot.
#RYPH_GITLAB_URL=https://gitlab.com
#RYPH_GITLAB_MODE=bot
#RYPH_GITLAB_TOKEN=
#RYPH_GITLAB_TOKEN_COMMAND=
# Sign-in and linking: an OAuth application (confidential, scope read_user, redirect URI
# <app origin>/gitlab/callback). Both or neither; the app's PUBLIC_GITLAB_CLIENT_ID matches it.
#RYPH_GITLAB_CLIENT_ID=
#RYPH_GITLAB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Who may sign up through GitLab: members of this group path. Unset: no group gate.
#RYPH_GITLAB_GROUP=

# ── Inbound webhooks ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The webhook mailroom (@ryph/webhooks) mounted in THIS process, because the App's webhook
# secret must not leave the forge's trust domain. GitHub signs each delivery, the mailroom
# verifies and queues it, and the consumer forwards a normalized event to the orchestrator.
# ALL THREE or none — the App above, the secret, and the database below: a webhook that cannot
# be verified, or an event nothing can act back on, is a trap rather than half a feature.
#
# The mailroom's own database on purpose — hook rows are hostile internet input, full bodies
# included, and do not belong beside anyone else's tables. Its schema is pushed separately, under
# the module's own variable — two names, and BOTH must resolve to the SAME database. A relative
# pglite path resolves against the directory each command runs in, so the push spells the forge's
# ./data/webhooks from its own directory:
#   RYPH_WEBHOOKS_DB=pglite:../forge/data/webhooks bun run --filter '@ryph/webhooks' db:push
#RYPH_FORGE_DB=pglite:./data/webhooks
# The secret configured on the App's webhook settings; every signature is checked against it.
#RYPH_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# GitLab (bot mode): the master each project's webhook token is derived from,
# hex(HMAC-SHA256(secret, "gitlab-hook:" + project id + ":" + generation)), so a leaked token
# forges events for its own project only, until its generation is rotated from the repo page.
# Deliveries land on /v1/hooks/gitlab?project=<id>&generation=<n>; one without a generation is
# refused. Needs the database above too.
#RYPH_GITLAB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Limits ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ceiling on a single upload-pack response served to a cloning run.
#RYPH_FORGE_MAX_UPLOAD_PACK_BYTES=10485760
# Ceiling on an accepted patch bundle.
#RYPH_FORGE_MAX_BUNDLE_BYTES=104857600

# ── Logging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# debug / info / warn / error / critical.
#RYPH_LOG_LEVEL=info
# json / text / colorful (default depends on whether stdout is a tty).
#RYPH_LOG_FORMAT=
